.TH YT-DLP-ARIA2-DOWNLOADER-GUI 1 "" "yt-dlp aria2 downloader" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yt-dlp-aria2-downloader-gui \- Zenity interface for yt-dlp aria2 downloader
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yt-dlp-aria2-downloader-gui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yt-dlp-aria2-downloader-gui
starts the Zenity graphical interface. It lets the user select a download
profile and destination, then supervises a single
.BR yt-dlp-aria2-downloader (1)
session with progress reporting and cancellation.
.PP
For youtube.com, youtu.be, youtube-nocookie.com, and their subdomains, the menu
offers exactly YouTube video - Firefox cookies (HLS/MKV) and Audio track (native
format). Every other normalized host offers exactly Complete video (MKV) and
Audio track (native format).
.PP
On compatible sites, complete-video requests analyse the available tracks before
transfer. Two checklists follow: choose one or more Audio tracks, then choose
Subtitles independently. The first subtitle row is No subtitles. Each window
has only Cancel and Continue. Continuing from the subtitle window starts the
transfer. No subtitles, or leaving every subtitle row unchecked, produces a
file with no subtitle tracks and skips subtitle downloads, conversion and
embedding.
Choose No subtitles or one or more subtitle tracks. Checking both is a conflict:
the application asks you to correct the selection before downloading.
.PP
The initial audio selection prefers a reliably identified original version.
If the original version is unknown, it chooses French, then the site's default
or another ordinary audio track, and explains this fallback in the window.
The default audio belongs to the selected tracks. When several audio tracks are
checked, the original remains the default if included. After Continue in the
audio window, the initial subtitle selection follows the selected default audio:
none for French, full French subtitles for another reliably identified language
when uniquely available, otherwise none with an explanation in the window.
Both checklists remain editable.
.PP
The lists contain only distinct admissible tracks after filtering and
deduplication. Check every desired track to include several languages or all
available tracks. Hearing-impaired subtitles and explicitly identified comfort
audio are excluded, including from initial selections. The CLI's all-track
option applies the same exclusions. Audio description remains a separate
available category. Full and forced subtitles remain distinct and
selectable in the player; forced passages never replace a full translation.
The validated MKV contains one video and exactly the selected audio and
subtitles without video or audio re-encoding. UTF-8 SRT preserves text, line
breaks and timing, but not source positioning. Unsupported formatting or timing
causes an explicit error. Availability depends on the programme, territory and
rights. Missing selected tracks are never silently replaced; incompatible
selections cannot resume older partial files.
.PP
A remembered audio profile stays selected. All other saved values, including
missing, invalid or incompatible preferences, select YouTube HLS video for
YouTube and complete video for other sites. The command-line engine continues
to support ordinary video mode for YouTube.
.PP
Progress includes percentage, speed, estimated time remaining and processing
phases, including the final destination copy. Local workspace details remain
in the diagnostic log. Errors with a safely retained diagnostic offer direct
View log and Close actions.
.SH SHARED DESTINATIONS
Independent GUI and CLI instances may transfer and process media concurrently
in the same folder. Final files appear directly there. Overlapping filename
families are refused with status 75; existing final files or unowned native
inputs are preserved with status 1. No numeric suffix is added automatically.
.PP
Reservations cover the same user and host, including canonical path aliases.
They remain held through consumer shutdown and cleanup. Native resume requires
an unchanged ownership checkpoint from a confirmed stop; a .part name alone is
insufficient. Uncertain shutdown preserves active state for manual inspection.
A verified filesystem identity separates a recreated directory from an older
checkpoint when its inode number is reused. Missing identity information does
not authorize releasing an older active checkpoint.
Do not delete old-looking lock files. The shared legacy lock excludes an older
2.3.29 instance's exclusive lock. This is not distributed exclusion and does
not cover arbitrary external writers.
.SH PROCESS SUPERVISION
Linux pidfds, WNOWAIT and readable process/thread inventories in procfs are
required in addition to Bash 4.4 and Python 3.10. The application checks their
operation on a private disposable child before media work; unavailable
capabilities cause an early refusal with status 69. A later observation or
permission failure preserves resources and does not establish complete shutdown.
A zombie thread leader with live sibling threads is still an active consumer.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/yt-dlp-aria2-downloader/gui.conf
Default GUI configuration file when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is not set.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/yt-dlp-aria2-downloader/download-*.log
Default retained GUI diagnostic-log pattern when
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
is not set. Each sanitized log ends with its exact basename and canonical
absolute path; the identity section and retained payload together remain within
the 8 MiB limit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yt-dlp-aria2-downloader (1),
.BR zenity (1)
